Everyone wants to enter into heaven
but heaven wants to come inside of you. 

We stand by the beachside and watch the waves 
wash the sand off your feet like ancient servants.

Every word is a slice of stolen apples.

This is our country. Our country has no name, 
only borders. What is inside of us none of us
can carry. So we lock hands to lighten the burden.

We stand on the white sand like proud parents
watching the strangeness between us walk 
for the first time.

A man dives into the sea and swims
towards the moon like a lifeguard. 

Kisses on your forehead are wave signals 
from another country rushing to the antenna 
of a transistor radio.

